// === ESP32-S3-EYE blob tracker — urbiscript-driven cycle + tracking ===
//
// Flat-list flavour: avoids two v0.7.x runtime bugs encountered while
// developing the richer class-based version (see design-risks.md):
//
//   1. "nested function/method call as arg to outer call silently
//      elides outer call" — breaks `List.new(Color.new().init(...), ...)`
//      construction (the outer List.new returns the LAST inner result
//      instead of wrapping them all in a List).
//
//   2. "chunk-top `var` interaction with at-handler body closure"
//      (suspected) — using chunk-top var pre-binding as a workaround
//      for (1) leaves at-body strands with NULL `s->module`, crashing
//      the first time any body fires (LoadProhibited at offset 0x0c).
//
// Both bugs are documented in docs/urbi-embedded-design-risks.md +
// REVIVAL.md §14 S42 (planned).  This script uses only literal-arg
// List.new(...) calls (no inline nested constructor calls) and avoids
// chunk-top `var` declarations to stay clear of both.
//
// The reactive runtime is still demonstrated through:
//   - Two chained at(blob_seen?) handlers (crosshair update + counter)
//   - Three chained at(button_pressed?) handlers (advance + apply + log)
//   - All state on Realm slots; no host-side cycle logic
//
// v0.7.1 lex/emit notes already documented in eye_demo history:
//   * No `[...]` list literal -- use List.new(...) + .get(i).
//   * No `&&`/`||` shortcut operators -- nested `if`.
//   * No `%` modulo operator -- wrap table via List.new(1, 2, 0).
//   * Async at-bodies must be direct calls or simple assignments;
//     `function () { ... }` bodies silently fail (R[0] payload
//     threading gap, design-risks row 14).  Chained handlers
//     (multiple `at (e?)` on the same event) work in install order
//     since S39 (commit ef647a7) widened PENDING_REFIRE to a bounded
//     counter.

// === Realm state =========================================================
//
// Parallel lists indexed by current_color_index.  When the BOOT
// button fires button_pressed, the chain advances the index using a
// next-table (replaces the missing `%` operator), reads the four
// channel values + tolerance + name at that index, and pushes them
// into the camera/log via host fns.
//
// Targets are pulled OFF the pure-saturated corner because real RGB565
// output of "red/green/blue" objects shows ~5-15 units of sensor noise
// + AWB leak on the "should be zero" channels.  Pure (31,0,0)/tol=4
// matches almost nothing on a live feed; the wider centres below catch
// most real objects under typical lighting.
Realm.color_names = List.new("RED", "GREEN", "BLUE");
Realm.color_r     = List.new(24,  6,  6);
Realm.color_g     = List.new( 6, 48,  6);
Realm.color_b     = List.new( 6,  6, 24);
Realm.color_tol   = List.new(12, 16, 12);

// Wrap table: index N maps to index (N+1) mod 3.  Replaces `%`.
Realm.next_color_index    = List.new(1, 2, 0);
Realm.current_color_index = 0;

// Counter incremented on every blob_seen event.  Read in the button
// chain's final log handler so each press dumps "total blobs: N" —
// gives the user an at-a-glance signal that blob detection is still
// running between presses.
Realm.blob_count = 0;

// === Boot announcement ===================================================
log("eye_demo loaded - BOOT cycles RED -> GREEN -> BLUE");

// === BLOB SEEN -- two chained at-handlers ================================
//
// destructure_blob (eye_demo_main.c) runs on the urbi task at
// safepoint drain and writes the centroid into Realm.last_blob_x /
// _y / _area.  These two at-handlers fire in install order on each
// blob event:
//
//   1. update crosshair (host fn writes the volatile pair the display
//      task overlays on the next frame);
//   2. increment the global blob counter.
//
// Two strand spawns per blob event x 25 Hz camera = 50 strand spawns/sec.
// Per spawn the body runs ~5-10 bytecode dispatch ops.  Light load,
// healthy steady-state strand pool = 0.
at (blob_seen?) draw_crosshair(Realm.last_blob_x, Realm.last_blob_y);
at (blob_seen?) Realm.blob_count = Realm.blob_count + 1;

// === BUTTON CYCLE -- three chained at-handlers ===========================
//
// Pure-urbiscript state machine.  Handler order is intentional:
//
//   1. Advance the wrap-table index (modulo 3 via next_color_index).
//   2. Push the new colour through set_target_color (host fn touches
//      the camera task's critical section under portMUX).
//   3. Log the new colour name + total blob count for visibility.
//
// log() is variadic + multi-type (UVAL_STR / UVAL_INT / UVAL_FLOAT /
// UVAL_BOOL / UVAL_NIL) so `log("target =>", name)` produces a single
// space-separated line "target => RED".
at (button_pressed?) Realm.current_color_index = Realm.next_color_index.get(Realm.current_color_index);
at (button_pressed?) set_target_color(
    Realm.color_r.get(Realm.current_color_index),
    Realm.color_g.get(Realm.current_color_index),
    Realm.color_b.get(Realm.current_color_index),
    Realm.color_tol.get(Realm.current_color_index));
at (button_pressed?) log("target =>",
    Realm.color_names.get(Realm.current_color_index),
    "total blobs:",
    Realm.blob_count);
